        "en": "When I was brought into the presence of Al-Rashid, I greeted him and he returned the greeting. Then he said, 'O Musa ibn Ja'far! Are there two Caliphs so that taxes must be collected twice?' I said, 'O Commander of the Faithful! I seek refuge in God that you should bear my sin and your sin, and that the falsehood of our enemies should be accepted against us. You know that lies have been told about us since the demise of the Messenger of God (peace be upon him and his family), and that knowledge is with you. If you see fit, due to your kinship with the Messenger of God, to permit me, I will narrate to you a hadith that my father told me, from his forefathers, from their grandfather, the Messenger of God (peace be upon him and his family).' He said, 'I have permitted you.' I said, 'My father told me, from his forefathers, from their grandfather, the Messenger of God (peace be upon him and his family), that he said: When kin touches kin, it moves and trembles. Give me your hand - may God make me your ransom!' He said, 'Come closer.' I came closer to him. He took my hand, then pulled me to himself and embraced me for a long time before letting me go. He said, 'Sit, O Musa, there is no harm upon you.' I looked at him and saw that his eyes were weeping. He returned to himself and said, 'You are truthful and your grandfather is truthful. My blood moved and my veins trembled until tenderness overcame me and my eyes overflowed. I want to ask you about things that have been churning in my chest for a while, which I have not asked anyone about. If you answer me, I will release you and not accept anyone's word against you. I have been told that you have never lied, so be truthful to me about what is in my heart.' I said, 'Whatever knowledge I have, I will inform you if you grant me immunity.' He said, 'You have immunity if you are truthful and leave the taqiyyah (concealment) by which you, O people of Fatima, are known.' I said, 'Let the Commander of the Faithful ask whatever he wishes.' He said, 'Tell me, why are you preferred over us while we are from the same tree and the children of Abdul Muttalib? We and you are one. We are the children of Al-Abbas and you are the children of Abu Talib, and both were uncles of the Messenger of God (peace be upon him and his family), and their kinship with him is equal?' I said, 'We are closer.' He said, 'How is that?' I said, 'Because Abdullah and Abu Talib were from one father and one mother, but your father Al-Abbas was not from the mother of Abdullah nor from the mother of Abu Talib.' He said, 'Why do you claim that you inherited the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) while the uncle blocks the son of the uncle, and the Messenger of God (peace be upon him and his family) was taken while Abu Talib had died before him and Al-Abbas his uncle was alive?' I said to him, 'If the Commander of the Faithful sees fit to excuse me from this question and ask me about any other door he wishes,' he said, 'No, or you must answer.' I said, 'Then grant me immunity.' He said, 'I have granted you immunity before the speech.' I said, 'In the saying of Ali ibn Abi Talib (peace be upon him): There is no share for anyone with the direct descendants (male or female) except for the parents, the spouse, and the wife, and no inheritance is established for the uncle with the direct descendants, and the Book does not mention it, except that Taym, Adiy, and the Umayyads said: The uncle is like the father, by their opinion without reality and without a report from the Messenger (peace be upon him and his family). And whoever of the scholars says the saying of Ali (peace be upon him), his ruling is contrary to the ruling of these. This is Nuh ibn Durraj who says in this matter the saying of Ali (peace be upon him) and has ruled by it, and the Commander of the Faithful appointed him governor of the two provinces, Kufa and Basra, and he ruled by it, and it was conveyed to the Commander of the Faithful. He ordered his bringing and the bringing of those who say contrary to his saying, from them Sufyan al-Thawri, Ibrahim al-Madani, and al-Fudayl ibn Ayad. They testified: That it is the saying of Ali (peace be upon him) in this matter. He said to them, as some of the scholars of Hijaz informed me: Why do you not rule by it when Nuh ibn Durraj has ruled by it? They said: Nuh was bold and we were timid. And the Commander of the Faithful approved a ruling, saying the predecessors of the general public from the Prophet (peace be upon him and his family) said: "

